	The coalgebraic signature of skip-free \textsf{GKAT}\xspace is the functor \(G\), where for any set \(X\), any \(f : X \to Y\), any \(\theta \in GX\), and any atomic test \(\alpha \in \mathsf{At}\),
	\begin{gather*}
		GX = (\bot + \Sigma\times(\checkmark + X))^{\mathsf{At}}
		\qquad
		G(f)(\theta)(\alpha) = \begin{cases}
			(p, f(x)) & \theta(\alpha) = (p, x) \\
			(p, \checkmark) &\theta(\alpha) = (p, \checkmark) \\
			\bot &\theta(\alpha) = \bot
		\end{cases}
	\end{gather*}
	The coalgebraic signature of one-free star behaviours is \(P\)~\cite{starmfps}, where for any set \(X\) and any \(U \subseteq (\mathsf{At} \cdot \Sigma) \times (\checkmark + X)\),
